Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: test A14 USB-A controller domain retention

USB-A works after pm_test=devices, but pm_test=platform reproduces SMMU
stream 0xda0 write translation faults and xHCI Host System Error, without
entering actual s2idle. A prior XHCI_RESET_ON_RESUME experiment timed out
and caused watchdog/RCU stalls; it is removed from this experiment.

The a400000 multiport controller uses GCC_USB30_MP_GDSC. Unlike the USB-C
domains retained by the existing patch set, this domain can power off in
the genpd noirq path. Test keeping only this controller domain on, gated
to the A14 board. The existing generic PM domain code then skips domain
power-off. Device clocks, PHY domains and xHCI PM callbacks are unchanged.

This is a power-retention workaround experiment, not a proven root-cause
fix. It may increase runtime and suspend power. It does not establish
whether DMA state, context retention, or power sequencing is responsible.
Disable at boot with gcc_glymur.a14_usba_keep_power=0.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-glymur.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/clk-provider.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 
@@ -7803,6 +7804,19 @@
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
+};
+
+/* A14-only alternate descriptor, selected before domain registration. */
+static struct gdsc gcc_usb30_mp_a14_gdsc = {
+	.gdscr = 0x9a010,
+	.en_rest_wait_val = 0x2,
+	.en_few_wait_val = 0x2,
+	.clk_dis_wait_val = 0xf,
+	.pd = {
+		.name = "gcc_usb30_mp_gdsc",
+	},
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | ALWAYS_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc gcc_usb30_prim_gdsc = {
@@ -8573,8 +8587,21 @@
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, gcc_glymur_match_table);
 
+/* Probe-time only: generic power-domain flags must not change live. */
+static bool a14_usba_keep_power = true;
+module_param(a14_usba_keep_power, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(a14_usba_keep_power,
+        "Keep the A14 USB-A controller power domain on for suspend diagnosis");
+
 static int gcc_glymur_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
+	if (a14_usba_keep_power &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407na")) {
+		gcc_glymur_gdscs[GCC_USB30_MP_GDSC] = &gcc_usb30_mp_a14_gdsc;
+		dev_info(&pdev->dev,
+			 "A14-USBA-power: keeping gcc_usb30_mp_gdsc on (experimental)\n");
+	}
+
 	return qcom_cc_probe(pdev, &gcc_glymur_desc);
 }
 
